{
  "kanji": "流",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 流\ntitle: flow\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-3, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 10\nradical: 水\nradicalNumber: 85\nonyomi: [リュウ, ル]\nkunyomi: [なが.れる, なが.れ, なが.す, -なが.す]\ndistractors: [泳, 活, 法]\n---\n\n# 流 — flow\n\n**Strokes:** 10 · **Key (radical):** 水 (as 氵, no. 85) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n流 expresses flowing or a current. [流れる](../words/流れる.md) ながれる describes the flow itself;\n流す (ながす) can mean letting something flow.\n交流 (こうりゅう), exchange or interaction, gives a useful compound beyond literal water.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** follow the three descending strokes at the lower right like\nseparate streams. The water form 氵 on the left reinforces this visual reminder, not a historical claim.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| なが.れる / なが.す | kun | [流れる](../words/流れる.md) ながれる — flow; 流す ながす — let flow |\n| リュウ | on | 交流 こうりゅう — exchange; interaction |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [流れる](../words/流れる.md) ながれる — flow\n- 流す ながす — let flow; drain\n- 交流 こうりゅう — exchange; interaction\n\n## Notes\n\n水が流れる (みずがながれる) means \"water flows\"; 水を流す (みずをながす) means\n\"let the water run.\" The が/を contrast helps keep the two verbs apart.\nDo not confuse the three lower-right strokes with the two spreading legs of [洗](洗.md).\n",
